  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 10, P = 28. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[24, 4, 9, 10, 17, 25, 26, 8, 10, 7], [17, 12, 22, 7, 1, 15, 26, 14, 24, 12], [8, 14, 0, 3, 9, 5, 2, 25, 25, 21]], sigma = [3, 4, 7, 0, 1, 8, 9, 2, 5, 6], B = [25, 3, 24, 25, 3, 22, 7, 24, 22, 7].",
  "references": [
